      "title": "Not Fooling Yourself",
      "gist": "The first principle is not to fool yourself, the easiest person to fool, and science has learned this slowly, as Millikan's electron charge history shows, though nobody teaches it.",
      "question": "Self-deception — how do scientists end up fooling themselves, and what can stop it? (a historical example)"
    },
